Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 10:42:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04830/11362] [outer-loop] MuSR energy-verifier: correct
 over-claim per adversarial review (judge>SC is NOT significant)

Adversarial sub-agent review (APPROVE) caught one over-claim: "MuSR HAS verifier headroom, REAL" leaned on
a noise-level judge result. McNemar exact: judge vs SC p=0.508, energy vs SC p=0.508 -> at n=50 NO method
significantly beats SC. Corrected the artifact + note: the cheap prompted decomposed-energy verifier is a
clean null (-0.06, CI incl 0); the LLM-judge is +0.06 but within sampling noise (p~=0.51); INCONCLUSIVE at
n=50, do NOT conclude "headroom is real" OR "energy can't help off-ARC". Decisive next lever = replicate at
n>=200 before carrying any formulation to ARC. Also added the _match_choice substring-trap code comment
(harmless on MuSR -- no overlapping option strings -- but harden before reuse). Review confirmed:
oracle-distinct (gold never reaches any scorer), faithfully implemented, informative null, tautology a
genuine small-n coincidence, parsing unbiased for this data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
